b41481112f6ca380fd31d51c892e7d3527b0baae0","event_uuid":"f5075d0d-9a2a-41f3-b8af-f0019a257776","position":{"commit_sha":"25b3f905106cab93696215a796033e9eca782bea","position":"1788908718749400001-f5075d0d-9a2a-41f3-b8af-f0019a257776"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Independent review PASS for commit 7a253b8c439b9895242ce8d446f53b7d812f43db. The leaf-linked receipt in session log vapourific-voracious-nerka contains exactly 65 unique PASS rows, one per allowlisted block, with immutable and final citations, preserved contracts, directive checks, and strictly lower word counts. Total audited prose fell from 4691 to 1747 words. Stage 1 spec compliance PASS, architecture compliance PASS. Stage 2 code quality PASS with no findings. Stage 3 domain integrity PASS with no domain-model changes. Local full-suite verification was intentionally deferred to Gerrit CI under the operator's documentation-only direction.","timestamp":1788818867289223839},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Independent exact-SHA documentation review PASS for corrective commit 1b5976cc383a55ef9f07e79b20e8d4fe4444ae45 (parent abb3d824365311cef2d159b25298d50dce04652c; tree 42a7ed050887a652a861a6ab59c4e5c572ab254e). All 65 changed prose blocks across 8 files passed factual, ownership, policy, and runtime checks with no findings. DDs passed: immutable-prose-only, exact-leaf-paths, diff-integrity, focused-contracts (276 tests), and comment-hygiene; commit-hook lint/typecheck passed, while user-waived full make verify was not run. Report SHA-256 421ff428cda1bd0fe9e74df8837db78415d4848791b14a67a09ed5d8eca10e05; receipt SHA-256 a5b5dd98feb179b9f4f7b974c541207764c382396569b5bc22976154a582ff1b. Gerrit 2820 reports merged but its revision is absent from current main; this corrective commit has a fresh Change-Id and restores only the ticket-owned comment/docless prose.","timestamp":1788902567215254001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction to the preceding evidence comment: the final phrase is comment/docstring prose.","timestamp":1788903747647368001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 2851 patch set 1 reached LLM-Review +1 with zero unresolved comments, but CI run 34280297343 failed in the py3.13 gating cell. The sole failure was tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py::test_sweep_extra_parity_would_have_caught_c57057f41: the test invokes git show c57057f41:.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml while the Gerrit checkout is fetch-depth 1, so the historical object is absent. CI otherwise reported 20,171 passed and 82 skipped. This is deterministic and independent of the comment-only patch, so no blind recheck was requested. Filed porcine-epicentral-cuscus for the separate debug session and linked it as this ticket’s blocker.","timestamp":1788908682254507001}],"created_at":1788570666375825464,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3aae0283-1ef9-4da5-bfb9-eae089438f4a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1e97-c19e-844a-4f66"},{"link_uuid":"c9a8a372-d703-4579-a988-acc33a5aa0e7","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1e13-bcea-cdaf-403b"},{"link_uuid":"0763a1b0-3806-49a2-902e-f57bae5d3817","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"2854-fc8a-aa2e-4b94"},{"link_uuid":"f8d13266-18e0-4f46-95ab-bf11c2b9e777","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"48fa-3d10-f9c8-4bed"},{"link_uuid":"0c88a644-1e99-483b-b4c6-12d77bf0e838","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"7511-1497-7103-4ed0"},{"link_uuid":"280297e0-7745-4890-aefb-c0a593e7f0cd","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"dc2c-0c03-da94-4144"},{"link_uuid":"625d862e-946b-41a4-a9ce-1514a82682c6","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"fb2b-8cea-83b1-46be"},{"link_uuid":"cd9df586-1e27-4101-b069-c1beb9b80a3b","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ce2e-b265-0613-486e"},{"link_uuid":"fb5244bb-17fc-4a26-98fa-5c616971dcf3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"},{"link_uuid":"a3bc80c2-dc12-4918-918f-a55ff961ac03","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d08f-9714-148d-4efa"},{"link_uuid":"8bb28ea4-7da1-46ca-8b08-38c75c55d504","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1e8a-a02d-b748-487a"}],"description":"## Context / immutable audit base\nAt d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84, these 8 declared files contain 65 confirmed comment/docstring blocks that can be shortened without changing behavior. The prior plan used broad ranges pinned to an older tree; those ranges mixed prose with executable code, concise explanations, and directives, and omitted later bloated blocks. Lines below are citations at the immutable base, never edit coordinates.\n\n## Exact prose allowlist\nA stable ID is the full path plus :: plus the listed suffix. Only these blocks may change.\n\n- src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py (17): module-docstring@1-13; module::comment(Registry route authority)@24-26; module::comment(Store-mount exclusions)@28-32; module::comment(Pure-intercept mount coverage)@34-37; _store_mount_eligible-docstring@42-52; _bridge_probe-docstring@88-104; _bridge_suggest_mapping-docstring@115-126; _suggest_mapping_write-docstring@187-192; module::comment(Pre-extracted confirmation flags)@290-298; main::comment(Removed-input boundary)@361-364; main::comment(Config-error boundary)@375-378; main::comment(Read-core exit ownership)@382-385; _main_dispatch::comment(Help pre-scan before effects)@395-399; _main_dispatch::comment(Global config overrides)@404-407; _main_dispatch::comment(One authoritative operation snapshot)@427-437; _main_dispatch::comment(Central store-mount gate)@441-447; _main_dispatch::comment(Real-command dispatch after pre-scan)@451-455.\n- src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py (6): module-docstring@1-23; module::comment(Nested help families)@33-36; wants_help-docstring@64-70; help_requested-docstring@80-85; _strip_config_prefix-docstring@112-117; pre_scan-docstring@154-159.\n- src/rebar/_cli/_init.py (8): module-docstring@1-17; _create_tracker-docstring@55-69; _create_tracker::comment(Auto-attach an existing tickets branch)@80-83; _confirm_and_init-docstring@107-124; ensure_initialized-docstring@152-159; ensure_initialized::comment(Use the configured tracker location)@168-171; ensure_store_mounted_best_effort-docstring@189-212; ensure_store_mounted_best_effort::comment(No-repo commands must not fail)@221-223.\n- src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py (4): module-docstring@1-20; _detect-docstring@43-54; _prompt_value-docstring@62-67; jira_onboard::comment(Collect all input before writing)@120-122.\n- src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py (17): module-docstring@1-8; module::comment(Eval/config cluster re-export)@16-19; _admission_refusal-docstring@27-32; _gate_source_error-docstring@39-42; _disposition_exit_code-docstring@104-109; _disposition_exit_code::comment(Signable PASS persistence failure)@123-129; _review_code::comment(Session-scoped review artifact)@162-167; _verify_completion::comment(Record standalone completion)@269-271; _verify_completion::comment(Verifier fault is retryable)@281-285; _review_plan-docstring@321-329; _review_plan::comment(Exact retry eligibility)@334-336; _review_plan::comment(Host congestion is retryable)@377-380; _sign_review-docstring@406-414; _render_step_failures-docstring@442-445; _render_reuse_notation-docstring@459-466; _render_plan_review_text::comment(Render indeterminate reason and remedy)@509-511; _render_plan_review_text::comment(Disclose capped advisory tail)@538-540.\n- src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/_common.py (2): module-docstring@1-12; _positive_int-docstring@20-26.\n- src/rebar/_cli/_registry_checks.py (4): module-docstring@1-19; module::comment(Capability vocabulary)@32-38; module::comment(Adapter vocabulary)@41-47; module::comment(Init-policy vocabulary)@52-55.\n- src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py (7): module-docstring@1-17; module::comment(Public registry exports)@32-36; Route::comment(Cross-session warning policy)@80-82; Route::comment(Execution metadata)@88-90; _intercepts::comment(Pure-intercept membership)@414-419; _intercepts::comment(Lazy handler metadata)@441-445; route_for-docstring@628-637.\n\n## Contracts, consumers, and exclusions\nPreserve registry-as-routing-authority, help/overview/unknown pre-scan before configuration or effects, global override precedence, exactly one bound operation snapshot, store-mount exclusions and ordering, and all stdout/stderr/exit-code shapes. Preserve automatic attachment versus explicit first-store consent, configured tracker-root resolution, and best-effort mount boundaries. Preserve Jira configuration precedence and presence-only secret handling. Preserve LLM admission/source error classes, retryable versus judgement exits, signing/sidecar persistence, retry eligibility, reuse notation, and uncapped-result disclosure. Preserve parser InvalidInputError ownership and the registry's closed capability/adapter/init vocabularies, aliases, lazy handlers, policy sets, and deterministic lookup. Consumers are CLI users and scripts plus library/MCP lifecycle adapters and generated help/reference parity tests. No allowlisted docstring feeds argparse help; all committed help bytes and runtime error/help strings remain exact.\n\nConcise or load-bearing prose outside the allowlist stays byte-identical. So do every runtime string, assertion, fixture, decorator, command argument, config key/value, and physical directive/shebang line. Repository-wide __doc__/inspect.getdoc census found no programmatic consumer of an allowlisted docstring.\n\n## Verification and independent review\nCompare each final file to d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84. For Python, parse with type_comments=True, replace only leading docstrings owned by the allowlisted Module/ClassDef/FunctionDef/AsyncFunctionDef owners, normalize only ast.TypeIgnore.lineno, and require the remaining AST/runtime tree to match. A zero-context diff-hunk guard permits changes only inside the cited base spans; directive/shebang physical lines must match exactly. Run the structured focused, path, hygiene, diff, and untimed repository commands.\n\nA reviewer who did not author the patch records a leaf-linked TSV with one PASS row per edited block (65 total): stable_id, before_citation, final_citation, preserved_contract_or_consumer, directives_exact, before_words, final_words, reviewer_session, semantic_pass, bloat_pass. Every final_words value must be smaller; missing, extra, or FAIL rows block closure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exactly the 65 allowlisted blocks are shortened; no other prose or directive changes.\n- [ ] The immutable-base prose-only oracle passes for all 8 files.\n- [ ] Every preserved contract above has a concrete independent-review PASS citation.\n- [ ] HEAD^..HEAD changes exactly the declared paths; focused checks, diff-check, hygiene, and make verify exit 0.\n- [ ] The independent TSV has exactly 65 complete PASS rows and proves a word-count reduction per block.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"Condense only 17 audited CLI routing, bridge, config, snapshot, mount, and error-boundary blocks while preserving dispatch order and output contracts."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py","reason":"Condense only 6 audited top-level help pre-scan blocks while preserving any-position help, config-prefix, and double-dash semantics."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_init.py","reason":"Condense only 8 audited auto-attach, consent, configured-root, freshness, and best-effort mount blocks while preserving initialization boundaries."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py","reason":"Condense only 4 audited Jira onboarding detection, prompt, and gather-before-write blocks while preserving precedence and secret handling."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","reason":"Condense only 17 audited LLM admission, disposition, persistence, retry, signing, and rendering blocks while preserving exact exit/result semantics."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/_common.py","reason":"Condense only 2 audited shared-parser converter blocks while preserving InvalidInputError and positive-integer contracts."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_registry_checks.py","reason":"Condense only 4 audited route-validation vocabulary blocks while preserving closed capability, adapter, and init-policy sets."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py","reason":"Condense only 7 audited route authority, export, policy, metadata, intercept, and lookup blocks while preserving lazy deterministic routing."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","d6eb-1c6c-88c3-48f6"],["relates_to","1e8a-a02d-b748-487a"],["relates_to","59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"],["relates_to","d08f-9714-148d-4efa"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"d6eb-1c6c-88c3-48f6","parent_status_uuid":"f5075d0d-9a2a-41f3-b8af-f0019a257776","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"blocked","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"0b6c-cf8e-a129-4e52","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in src/rebar/_cli","verify_commands":[{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c 'import ast, io, json, re, subprocess, tokenize\nfrom pathlib import Path\nB=\"d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84\"\nM=json.loads(\"\"\"{\"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py\":{\"docs\":[\"module\",\"_store_mount_eligible\",\"_bridge_probe\",\"_bridge_suggest_mapping\",\"_suggest_mapping_write\"],\"spans\":[[1,13],[24,26],[28,32],[34,37],[42,52],[88,104],[115,126],[187,192],[290,298],[361,364],[375,378],[382,385],[395,399],[404,407],[427,437],[441,447],[451,455]]},\"src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py\":{\"docs\":[\"module\",\"wants_help\",\"help_requested\",\"_strip_config_prefix\",\"pre_scan\"],\"spans\":[[1,23],[33,36],[64,70],[80,85],[112,117],[154,159]]},\"src/rebar/_cli/_init.py\":{\"docs\":[\"module\",\"_create_tracker\",\"_confirm_and_init\",\"ensure_initialized\",\"ensure_store_mounted_best_effort\"],\"spans\":[[1,17],[55,69],[80,83],[107,124],[152,159],[168,171],[189,212],[221,223]]},\"src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py\":{\"docs\":[\"module\",\"_detect\",\"_prompt_value\"],\"spans\":[[1,20],[43,54],[62,67],[120,122]]},\"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py\":{\"docs\":[\"module\",\"_admission_refusal\",\"_gate_source_error\",\"_disposition_exit_code\",\"_review_plan\",\"_sign_review\",\"_render_step_failures\",\"_render_reuse_notation\"],\"spans\":[[1,8],[16,19],[27,32],[39,42],[104,109],[123,129],[162,167],[269,271],[281,285],[321,329],[334,336],[377,380],[406,414],[442,445],[459,466],[509,511],[538,540]]},\"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/_common.py\":{\"docs\":[\"module\",\"_positive_int\"],\"spans\":[[1,12],[20,26]]},\"src/rebar/_cli/_registry_checks.py\":{\"docs\":[\"module\"],\"spans\":[[1,19],[32,38],[41,47],[52,55]]},\"src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py\":{\"docs\":[\"module\",\"route_for\"],\"spans\":[[1,17],[32,36],[80,82],[88,90],[414,419],[441,445],[628,637]]}}\"\"\")\nTOKENS=(\"noqa\",\"type:\",\"pyright:\",\"mypy:\",\"ruff:\",\"fmt:\",\"isort:\",\"pragma:\",\"nosec\",\"coverage:\",\"mechanism-ok:\",\"raw-git-ok:\",\"tickets-boundary-ok:\",\"read-via:\",\"repo-root-ok:\")\ndef normalize(src,path):\n    spec=M[path]\n    tree=ast.parse(src,filename=path,type_comments=True)\n    seen=set()\n    def walk(node,qual=\"module\"):\n        current=qual\n        if isinstance(node,(ast.ClassDef,ast.FunctionDef,ast.AsyncFunctionDef)):\n            current=node.name if qual==\"module\" else f\"{qual}.{node.name}\"\n        body=getattr(node,\"body\",[])\n        if isinstance(body,list) and current in spec[\"docs\"] and body and isinstance(body[0],ast.Expr) and isinstance(body[0].value,ast.Constant) and isinstance(body[0].value.value,str):\n            body[0].value.value=\"__ALLOWLISTED_PROSE__\"\n            seen.add(current)\n        for child in ast.iter_child_nodes(node):\n            walk(child,current)\n    walk(tree)\n    assert seen==set(spec[\"docs\"]),(\"missing allowlisted docstring\",path,sorted(set(spec[\"docs\"])-seen))\n    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n        if isinstance(node,ast.TypeIgnore):\n            node.lineno=0\n    return ast.dump(tree,include_attributes=False)\ndef directives(src):\n    lines=src.splitlines()\n    found=[]\n    for tok in tokenize.generate_tokens(io.StringIO(src).readline):\n        if tok.type!=tokenize.COMMENT:\n            continue\n        body=tok.string[1:].lstrip()\n        if tok.string.startswith(\"#!\") or any(body.startswith(prefix) for prefix in TOKENS):\n            found.append(lines[tok.start[0]-1])\n    return found\ndef runtime_yaml(src):\n    return [line for line in src.splitlines() if line.strip() and not line.lstrip().startswith(\"#\")]\ndef check_hunks(path):\n    diff=subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"diff\",\"--unified=0\",B,\"--\",path],text=True)\n    for line in diff.splitlines():\n        if not line.startswith(\"@@\"):\n            continue\n        match=re.match(r\"@@ -(\\d+)(?:,(\\d+))? \\+\\d+(?:,\\d+)? @@\",line)\n        assert match,(\"unparsed hunk\",path,line)\n        start=int(match.group(1)); count=1 if match.group(2) is None else int(match.group(2))\n        assert count>0,(\"addition-only hunk\",path,line)\n        end=start+count-1\n        assert any(start>=a and end<=b for a,b in M[path][\"spans\"]),(\"change outside allowlist\",path,line)\nfor path,spec in M.items():\n    before=subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"show\",f\"{B}:{path}\"],text=True)\n    final=Path(path).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    if spec.get(\"yaml\"):\n        assert runtime_yaml(before)==runtime_yaml(final),(\"YAML runtime drift\",path)\n    else:\n        assert normalize(before,path)==normalize(final,path),(\"AST/runtime drift\",path)\n        assert directives(before)==directives(final),(\"directive/shebang drift\",path)\n    check_hunks(path)'","dd_id":"immutable-prose-only","dd_text":"Only the 65 allowlisted prose blocks may change; normalized base/final Python ASTs and directive lines match, and every zero-context hunk deletes only allowlisted base lines."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c 'import json, subprocess; expected=set(json.loads(\"\"\"[\"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py\",\"src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py\",\"src/rebar/_cli/_init.py\",\"src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py\",\"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py\",\"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/_common.py\",\"src/rebar/_cli/_registry_checks.py\",\"src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py\"]\"\"\")); actual=set(subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"diff\",\"--name-only\",\"HEAD^..HEAD\"],text=True).splitlines()); assert actual==expected,{\"expected\":sorted(expected),\"actual\":sorted(actual)}'","dd_id":"exact-leaf-paths","dd_text":"The single ticket commit changes exactly the declared file-impact set."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py","dd_id":"comment-hygiene","dd_text":"The repository comment-hygiene policy passes."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest -q tests/interfaces/contracts/test_create_help_no_write_b8de.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_operation_snapshot_authoritative_binding.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py tests/unit/test_init_attach_predicate.py tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py tests/unit/test_llm_commands_render.py tests/unit/test_cli_registry.py tests/unit/test_cli_registry_dispatch.py tests/unit/test_core_cli_parsers.py tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes.py","dd_id":"focused-contracts","dd_text":"Focused tests for every preserved subsystem contract pass."},{"command":"rtk git diff --check HEAD^..HEAD -- src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py src/rebar/_cli/_init.py src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/_common.py src/rebar/_cli/_registry_checks.py src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py","dd_id":"diff-integrity","dd_text":"The path-scoped patch contains no whitespace errors."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify","dd_id":"repository-gates","dd_text":"The complete local CI contract passes in the worktree virtualenv; do not apply a timeout."}]},"source_event_uuids":["901fa869-c910-4721-a1c9-cc1dfe2368bd","d7a9a42a-025e-4377-b589-939d7ff586f5","3e0bfe63-aee5-4d67-b18d-4ddbbe042a6e","98da0bb1-2b6e-432d-9a55-9ca79c73b146","03ee43f2-a6eb-435a-ae6f-062e00c56bde","45240e4b-fb9a-4ebf-b7b1-7e050e5c62b2","bda3f5af-26d3-47cb-8426-2e41af5ee279","fb5244bb-17fc-4a26-98fa-5c616971dcf3","ea755384-3825-4420-b748-bfaccacf6747","a3bc80c2-dc12-4918-918f-a55ff961ac03","f980a76d-9e05-499a-b124-87cbedc95518","6fbca3c1-930a-467d-be61-0fd4b4782b79","8bb28ea4-7da1-46ca-8b08-38c75c55d504","ea918c7e-8c92-4094-96fb-8fd88f9a1062","f5075d0d-9a2a-41f3-b8af-f0019a257776"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788912437503140001,"uuid":"e8173ceb-bf90-47eb-a0b0-a9127253cc16"}